# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/modelExplainability node236
node236 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>modelExplainability</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/modelExplainability' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/modelExplainability</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Methods that can be used to explain the results from the AI model.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Methods that can be used to explain the results from the AI model.&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;A free-form text that lists the different explainability mechanisms and how
they can be used to explain the results from the AI model.

The mechanisms can be model-agnostic methods, such as
SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP) &lt;https://shap.readthedocs.io/&gt; and
Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations (LIME) &lt;https://github.com/marcotcr/lime&gt;,
and model-specific methods that applied to a limited category of models.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/AI/limitation node237
