# https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/isOsiApproved node1050
node1050 [ shape=none, color=black label=< <table color='#666666' cellborder='0' cellspacing='0' border='1'><tr><td colspan='2' bgcolor='grey'><B>isOsiApproved</B></td></tr><tr><td href='https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/isOsiApproved' bgcolor='#eeeeee' colspan='2'><font point-size='10' color='#6666ff'>https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/isOsiApproved</font></td></tr><tr><td align='left'>rdfs:comment</td><td align='left'>&quot;Specifies whether the License is listed as approved by the
Open Source Initiative (OSI).&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:definition</td><td align='left'>&quot;Specifies whether the License is listed as approved by the
Open Source Initiative (OSI).&quot;@en</td></tr><tr><td align='left'>skos:note</td><td align='left'>&quot;isOsiApproved specifies whether the
Open Source Initiative (OSI) &lt;https://opensource.org&gt;
has listed this License as &quot;approved&quot; in their list of OSI Approved Licenses,
located at the time of this writing at
OSI Approved Licenses &lt;https://opensource.org/licenses&gt;.

A value of &quot;true&quot; indicates that the license is in the list of licenses that
OSI publishes as approved.

A value of &quot;false&quot; indicates that the license is explicitly not in the
corresponding list of OSI licenses (e.g., OSI has stated publicly that a
license is not approved).

If the isOsiApproved field is not specified, the SPDX data creator makes no
assertions about whether the License is approved by the OSI.&quot;@en</td></tr></table> > ] 
